## About this package

Ready-to-use vision models for Emgu LiteRT that take Emgu CV images (`Emgu.CV.Mat`, 8-bit BGR). It is part of the ${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MAJOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_MINOR}.${CPACK_PACKAGE_VERSION_PATCH} release of Emgu LiteRT. It depends on the managed Emgu CV library; to deploy, also add an Emgu CV runtime package for your platform (`Emgu.CV.runtime.*`). `${EMGU_LITERT_MODELS_NUGET_ID}` itself has no Emgu CV dependency.

Detectors, on LiteRT's CompiledModel API (`Emgu.LiteRT`). Each downloads its weights on first use (`PrepareAsync`), then `Detect(Mat)`:

- `CocoDetector`: COCO SSD MobileNet V3, 80 COCO classes
- `YoloXDetector`: YOLOX-Nano
- `PicoDetDetector`: PP-PicoDet-S
- `DFineDetector`: D-FINE-N (CPU only, the most accurate and the slowest)
- `HandGestureDetector`: MediaPipe's hand landmarks and gestures
- `PoseDetector`: MediaPipe's pose landmarks (33 body landmarks)

On Android and Mac Catalyst a detector tries the GPU, keeps it only if it gives the CPU's results on a known image and is faster, and otherwise runs on the CPU. For that check pass `validationImage`, which returns bundled images by name (`surfers.jpg`, `hand_thumb_up.jpg`, `pose_standing.jpg`); without it the CPU is always used.

```csharp
using (var detector = new Emgu.LiteRT.Models.YoloXDetector(cacheDirectory: weightsFolder))
{
    await detector.PrepareAsync(preferGpu: false, numThreads: 4, progress: null, CancellationToken.None);
    using Mat image = CvInvoke.Imread("surfers.jpg");
    foreach (var r in detector.Detect(image))
        Console.WriteLine($"{r.Label}: {r.Score:P0}");
}
```

Depth from one photo: `DepthEstimator` runs Depth Anything V2 Small (Apache 2.0, a 27.7 MB download on first use; GPU at FP16 when it matches the CPU on `surfers.jpg` and is faster). `Estimate(Mat)` returns a float map the photo's size, 0 farthest to 1 nearest (relative, not metres), and `DepthEffects.BlurBackground(photo, depth)` gives the photo a portrait mode's look:

```csharp
using var depthEstimator = new Emgu.LiteRT.Models.DepthEstimator(cacheDirectory: weightsFolder);
await depthEstimator.PrepareAsync(preferGpu: false, numThreads: 4, progress: null, CancellationToken.None);
using Mat depth = depthEstimator.Estimate(image);
using Mat portrait = Emgu.LiteRT.Models.DepthEffects.BlurBackground(image, depth);
```

For the Interpreter-based `Mobilenet` and `Inception` of `Emgu.TF.Lite.Models`, `InterpreterMatInput` adds `Recognize(Mat)` and `WriteInput(Mat)`:

```csharp
using Emgu.TF.Lite.Models;
var best = mobilenet.Recognize(image)[0];
```

For online documentation please visit
